libsdl3 (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Carry Tomasz Pakuła's SDL pull request 14758
    (https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/pull/14758, open, two commits of
    2026-01-04, patches 0001 and 0002): a joystick on a kernel that has the
    EV_BTN event (kernel series group 44 of the edition, "Input: New EV_BTN
    event for generic buttons") reports every button the device has, so 128
    buttons arrive as 128 (without it Linux joysticks stop at 80 buttons, and
    SDL at 79). ORDER 15.
  * 0003: the pull request falls back to "#define EVIOCGBTNCNT 0" when the
    build headers lack EV_BTN, and ioctl(fd, 0, ...) always fails, so a library
    built before the headers carry EV_BTN never used the event. The real
    number is _IOR('E', 0x1c, unsigned int). Found with the 128-button
    fixture on an EV_BTN kernel.
  * 0004: when the kernel has no EV_BTN and a joystick uses the last key code
    (so it may have more buttons than the kernel numbers), SDL says so once
    when the joystick is opened; it dropped them in silence before.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@
